+# Implementation Plan: JSON Patch
+**Spec**: [spec.md](spec.md) — RFC 6902 §4, §5; RFC 6901 §3, §4.
+
+## Approach
+Single module addition in `src/index.ts`. Deep-clone the document once (own-property copying via `Object.defineProperty`, so `__proto__` stays an own member), apply operations to the clone, and return it; any throw discards the clone, which gives atomicity (§5). Values from `add`/`replace`/`copy`/`move` are cloned. Pointers are parsed with a shared tokenizer extracted from `resolvePointer` (same syntax errors). Errors: `JsonPatchError` (base, `index`), `JsonPatchInvalidError`, `JsonPatchOperationError`.
+
+## Constitution Check
+- I: RFC 6902 sections named; atomicity, move-prefix rule, `-`, test equality implemented as stated. PASS
+- II: no dependencies. PASS
+- III: tests first in `tests/patch.test.ts`, seen failing. PASS
+- IV: no mutation, clones, prototype-safe, typed errors. PASS
+- V: exported from entry, doc comments, strict TS, no `any`. PASS
+- VI: one function plus small helpers. PASS
